# The re-created incarnation's first initialisation seeds the floor plus one but
# claims nothing (#5668). After a new-build purge the WAL-side floor refuses a
# straddler without the claim (a redundancy there). After a purge that finished on
# 10.2.0, the catch-up raises only the floor row: the partition entries stay and a
# running WAL shard's in-memory floor is not raised, so a straddler of L's own shard
# root, stamped with the predating marker's generation, meets its entry and is
# admitted above the heads the initialisation recorded. There the claim is what
# refuses it.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRoutingInitWithoutClaim
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a re-created tree's marker reads initialised before its seeded generation is claimed
PERTURBS: MarkInit
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithLegacyPurge = TRUE, WithSecondInitiator = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
            /\ fFence' = Max2(fFence, Max2(fEpoch, rFloor + 1))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the initialisation claims nothing.
            /\ fFence' = fFence
--- END
